{"step_index":120,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:54:22Z","content":"Priyanshu, do seedhe sawaal hain, do seedhe jawab:\n\n## 1. Inverter vs UPS — Kya Problem Hogi?\n\n**Agar ghar pe inverter hai, toh UPS ki zaroorat nahi.** Mac mini sirf 10-15W khaata hai idle mein (phone charger jaisa). Inverter aaram se sambhal lega.\n\n| Situation | Kya hoga |\n|:---|:---|\n| **Bijli gayi, inverter ne switch kiya** | Mac mini chalu rahega. Modern inverters 5-20ms mein switch karte hain — Mac mini ko pata bhi nahi chalega |\n| **Inverter ka output** | Agar tera inverter **pure sine wave** hai (₹5,000+ wale) toh perfect. Square wave inverters mein sometimes electronics mein hum/noise aata hai, lekin Mac mini ke power adapter handle kar leta hai |\n| **Mac mini ka load** | Peak pe bhi 60W. Tera inverter 500W-1500W handle karta hoga. Mac mini ka load uske liye kuch bhi nahi hai |\n\n**Short answer: Inverter = kafi. UPS mat le alag se.**\n\n---\n\n## 2. Ghar Pe Internet Chahiye? Wi-Fi Lagwana Padega?\n\n**Haan. 100%. Bina internet ke remote access IMPOSSIBLE hai.**\n\nSamjha aise:\n\n```\nTu (Cafe mein, cafe ka Wi-Fi)\n    ↓ Internet\n    ↓ Tailscale VPN\n    ↓ Internet\nMac mini (Ghar pe, GHAR KA internet chahiye)\n```\n\n**Dono ends pe internet chahiye.** Tu cafe ka Wi-Fi use karega apni side se. Mac mini ghar ka Wi-Fi/broadband use karega apni side se. Dono online honge tabhi Tailscale connect karega.\n\n**Agar ghar pe internet nahi hai → Mac mini online nahi → tu remote access nahi kar payega. Simple.**\n\n### Kya chahiye ghar pe:\n\n| Cheez | Chahiye? | Kitna kharcha |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| **Broadband connection** | ✅ Haan, mandatory | ₹500-800/month (Jio Fiber, Airtel, BSNL — basic plan kafi hai) |\n| **Wi-Fi router** | ✅ Haan (mostly broadband ke saath free milta hai) | ₹0 (included) ya ₹1,000-2,000 alag se |\n| **Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se connect karna** | ✅ Haan — Mac mini mein Wi-Fi 7 built-in hai | ₹0 |\n| **Ethernet cable (optional)** | Better than Wi-Fi for always-on server | ₹200-500 (stable connection, recommended) |\n\n### Agar ghar pe already broadband hai:\n\nToh bas Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se connect kar, Tailscale install kar, Ollama setup kar — done. Koi extra kharcha nahi.\n\n### Agar ghar pe broadband NAHI hai:\n\nToh ₹500-800/month ka basic plan lagwa. Jio Fiber ka ₹399 wala plan bhi chalega — tujhe video streaming nahi karni Mac mini se, sirf text data (prompts + responses) jaayega jo 1-2 KB/sec hai. Sabse sasta internet plan bhi kaafi hai.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro tip:** Mac mini ko Wi-Fi se nahi, **Ethernet cable** se router se connect kar. Wi-Fi se bhi chalega, lekin Ethernet zyada stable hai — 24/7 server ke liye disconnect nahi hoga kabhi. Ek ₹200 ka LAN cable laga de, tension-free.","thinking":"The user is asking two simple, practical questions:\n\n1. If they have an inverter at home, do they need a UPS for the Mac mini? Will the inverter handle the power backup?\n2. Does the Mac mini need to be connected to the internet (Wi-Fi) at home for the user to access it remotely from a cafe/library? Do they need to get a Wi-Fi connection at home?\n\nThese are straightforward questions. Let me answer directly without over-researching.\n\n1. **Inverter vs UPS**: An inverter at home will work fine for keeping the Mac mini running during power cuts. The Mac mini uses very little power (10-15W idle, 40-60W under load). \n\nA regular inverter should handle this fine, though there's a brief switchover gap when mains cuts out that a true UPS avoids entirely with instant switching. Still, most modern inverters switch fast enough that the Mac mini won't even blink. For the second question, yes - the Mac mini absolutely needs to stay connected to the internet at home for remote access via Tailscale to work while they're out at a cafe.\n\nThese are straightforward questions, so I'll just answer directly without needing an artifact.\n\n"}
