{"step_index":122,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-01T12:59:03Z","content":"## Ethernet Cable Kyun? (2 Lines)\n\nWi-Fi sometimes raat ko 2 baje disconnect ho jaata hai — router restart hua, signal weak hua. Agar Mac mini Wi-Fi pe hai aur disconnect hua, toh tu cafe se access nahi kar payega. **Ethernet cable = physical wire jo router se Mac mini mein lagta hai. Ye kabhi disconnect nahi hota.** Bas itna. Haan, table aur pro tip dono same baat hai.\n\n---\n\n## Mac mini bina screen ke kaise chalega?\n\n**Koi problem nahi hai. Mac mini bina monitor, bina keyboard, bina mouse ke chal sakta hai.** Isko \"headless\" bolte hain — bahut common hai, log server ke liye exactly aise hi use karte hain.\n\nSetup ek baar karna padega (pehli baar monitor lagake):\n\n| Step | Kya karna hai | Ek baar ya hamesha |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| **1** | Mac mini pehli baar monitor + keyboard lagake setup kar — Apple ID, Wi-Fi/Ethernet, Ollama install | Ek baar |\n| **2** | System Settings → Energy → **\"Prevent automatic sleeping\"** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **3** | System Settings → General → Sharing → **\"Remote Login\" (SSH)** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **4** | System Settings → General → Sharing → **\"Screen Sharing\"** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **5** | System Settings → Energy → **\"Start up automatically after power failure\"** ON kar | Ek baar |\n| **6** | Monitor/keyboard nikal de. Mac mini chalta rahega bina screen ke | Done |\n\n**Ab kaise access karega bina screen ke:**\n\n| Kahan se | Kaise |\n|:---|:---|\n| **Ghar mein MacBook Air se** | Finder → Network → Mac mini dikhega → Screen Sharing se poora desktop dikha dega tere Air pe |\n| **Bahar se MacBook Air se** | Tailscale se connect kar → SSH ya Screen Sharing — same cheez, internet ke through |\n\nMac mini ko screen ki zaroorat nahi hai chalne ke liye. Wo background mein Ollama chala raha hai, internet se connected hai, aur tera prompt ka wait kar raha hai. Jaise tera Wi-Fi router bina screen ke 24/7 chalta hai — Mac mini bhi waise hi chalega.","thinking":"The user has thr